From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +1000
Subject: net: phy: realtek: move RTL826x firmware load to config_init

rtl8261n_probe() / rtl8264b_probe() call rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init()
which uses request_firmware_direct() and returns -EPROBE_DEFER when
rtl8261n.bin / rtl8264b.bin are not yet available (squashfs not mounted).
The kernel retries probe at ~1s intervals, delaying PHY attach by
several seconds.

Move firmware loading from probe() to config_init():

- Store the firmware filename in priv->fw_name at probe time.
- Call rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init() from rtl826x_config_init() when
  priv->patch is still NULL. By the time any network interface is
  brought up squashfs is guaranteed to be mounted, so the firmware is
  always available and -EPROBE_DEFER is never needed.
- Make rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init() non-static and export it for this use.

This is the trimmed-down successor to the original IRQ-race patch.
The VEND2:INER masking is unnecessary while DTS leaves interrupts
unwired on phy5/phy8 (the W1700K case).

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek.h
